Also a couple of things:

1. The Cloud Functions API is technically deprecated. Unless you plan on deploying or currently deploy your functions using the legacy API, I believe GCP now recommends using the Cloud Run API for function deployments.
2. We usually don't assign "admin" roles to service accounts, as it violates one of the NIST 800-53 compliance rules. I know that certain CI/CD pipelines might need to modify things such as resource IAM, so exceptions can be made for certain scenarios.
3. We also don't assign roles/serviceAccountUser on the project-level for the same reason as above. We usually don't make any exceptions for this case: people that need to "use" a service account need to be granted permissions on each individual service account.
4. We created a role for Drew to deploy serverless functions within winde-dev. Would you like to inherit those roles instead?

Reply:- 
1. cloud Functions v2 is NOT deprecated — it runs on Cloud Run internally. Only v1 is legacy.
2. For Eventarc we'll use eventarc.eventReceiver (not admin), and for Storage we'll use storage.objectAdmin (not 
   admin).
3. we'll grant serviceAccountUser at individual SA level, not project level


